# Build Your First Agent

This Livebook declares an Agent with an inline Action, a route default, and a
generated command interface. It then instantiates the declaration as an Agent
value.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Declare The Agent

Use an inline Action when the behavior is local to one Agent route. Extract a
named Action when other Agents or Flows must reuse it.

```elixir
defmodule FirstAgent.Counter do
  use Jido.Agent,
    name: "first_agent_counter",
    description: "Counts typed increment Signals"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{
             count: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.min(0) |> Zoi.default(0),
             last_amount: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)
           })
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/first-agent"

    route "counter.increment" do
      action %{amount: amount},
        name: "first_agent_increment",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{amount: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.min(0)}),
        context: context do
        state = context.agent_state

        {:ok,
         %{
           state
           | count: state.count + amount,
             last_amount: amount
         }}
      end

      defaults %{amount: 1}
      define :increment, args: [{:optional, :amount}]
    end
  end
end
```

The data schema supplies initial values. The Action input schema protects the
route input. The complete Agent data schema validates the returned state.

## Inspect The Definition

```elixir
definition = FirstAgent.Counter.agent()

%{
  definition?: Jido.Agent.definition?(definition),
  id: definition.id,
  state: definition.state,
  route_count: length(definition.routes)
}
```

A definition has no ID and no state. It is reusable authoring data.

## Instantiate The Agent

```elixir
agent = FirstAgent.Counter.new!(id: "counter-1")

%{
  instance?: Jido.Agent.instance?(agent),
  id: agent.id,
  state: agent.state
}
```

## Use The Generated Signal Helper

Omit the optional argument to use the route default.

```elixir
{:ok, default_signal} = FirstAgent.Counter.increment_signal()
{:ok, after_default, []} = FirstAgent.Counter.cmd(agent, default_signal)

{:ok, explicit_signal} = FirstAgent.Counter.increment_signal(4)
{:ok, after_explicit, []} = FirstAgent.Counter.cmd(after_default, explicit_signal)

after_explicit.state
```

The final state is `%{count: 5, last_amount: 4}`.

## Reject Invalid Input

```elixir
{:ok, invalid_signal} = FirstAgent.Counter.increment_signal(-1)
{:error, error} = FirstAgent.Counter.cmd(after_explicit, invalid_signal)

{error.__struct__, after_explicit.state.count}
```

The Action does not run, and the source Agent value stays at count five.

Continue with [Agent DSL](agent-dsl.livemd) and
[Route Interfaces](route-interfaces.livemd).
